{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK89Q1GmjaEV9KZtvPcA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`STATIC_URL` and `MEDIA_URL` now get the current `SCRIPT_NAME` prefix when they are relative. The change is in `django/conf/__init__.py`. I didn't write a test that serves a request under a `SCRIPT_NAME`, so the prefixing itself is unexercised.\n\n**What it does:** a value like `static/` becomes `<script prefix>static/`. Full URLs (`http://…`, `https://…`) and values starting with `/` are left alone. The prefix comes from `get_script_prefix()`, so it follows whatever `SCRIPT_NAME` the current request set. Those two settings are no longer cached on the settings object, so the prefix is recomputed on each access.\n\nThe `{% static %}` tag, `STATIC_URL`-based staticfiles storage and the default media storage all read the settings through this path, so they pick up the prefix without further edits.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `settings_tests` passes.\n- In `staticfiles_tests` and `file_storage`, two tests (the `StaticLiveServerView` class and `FileLikeObjectTestCase`) error in `setUpClass` when binding a server socket. They also error without my change.\n- Four `file_storage` `test_setting_changed` tests fail because `test_setting_changed` expects an overridden `MEDIA_URL` of `overridden_media_url/` and now gets `/overridden_media_url/`. A relative value now gets the script prefix, which defaults to `/`. I didn't edit the test, as the rules forbid it.\n\nOne limit: storage objects created while a request is running pick up that request's prefix when they are built. `StaticFilesStorage` and the cached `base_url` on `FileSystemStorage` then keep that prefix instead of recomputing it per request."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":526,"cache_read_input_tokens":27444,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemera